<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells 90,000/T March fuel oil at $103/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells 90,000/T March fuel oil at $103/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has sold by tender three 30,000-tonne March cargoes of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil at $103 per tonne free-on-board (fob) Taiwan, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The high sulphur cargoes are lifting March 12-28 from Kaohsiung, the official said.</p>
<p>CPC last awarded 30,000 tonnes of sulphur fuel oil at around $101 per tonne fob for February 18-27 lifting.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3571)</p>
